{% if agent_evaluation %}

You may measure your own workspace before you reply: call `submit_evaluation` on the
`evaluation` tool. The framework decides whether the submission is admitted and counts
a new candidate against the run's budget; a refusal names the reason, so change the
workspace or stop submitting. A candidate with the same content is evaluated once for
this workstream, whoever asks: if the implementer or the reviewer already submitted it,
the call returns that evaluation's handle (`"repeat": true`) and charges nothing. A
reply with an `outcome` is an evaluation that has already ended, and lists its `evidence`
ids as a resume would: do not wait for it. A successful call returns a handle. To wait for the
result, call `validate_evaluation_wait` with every handle you need, then finish the
turn with only `{"reply":{"kind":"waiting_for_evaluation","handles":["<handle>"]}}`. Do not
poll: the host resumes this same session once every listed measurement is terminal.
A waiting turn uses no new attempt.
{% endif %}
